Product Requirements and Purpose Document

Product Name: Bitcoin Trading Simulation Bot
Purpose
The purpose of this project is to develop a Python-based Bitcoin Trading Simulation Bot that simulates trading activities using real-time Bitcoin price data. The bot will execute simulated trades every 10 minutes based on a simple trading algorithm. This tool aims to provide insights into trading strategies without the risk of real financial loss. It serves as a foundation for developers to experiment with algorithmic trading and to potentially build more sophisticated systems in the future.

Scope
In Scope
Development of a Python application that:
Runs continuously and executes actions every 10 minutes.
Fetches real-time Bitcoin price data.
Simulates trades using a fictitious amount of capital.
Implements a basic trading algorithm based on current price trends.
Logs all simulated trades and portfolio performance.
Generates performance reports over a specified simulation period (e.g., one week).
Out of Scope
Execution of real trades involving actual money.
Support for cryptocurrencies other than Bitcoin.
Integration with live trading platforms or exchanges.
Advanced trading strategies involving AI or machine learning.
Graphical user interface (GUI) development.
Functional Requirements
Data Acquisition

The bot shall fetch real-time Bitcoin price data at regular intervals (every minute).
Use a reliable and publicly available API (e.g., CoinGecko API, Binance API).
Handle API rate limits and exceptions gracefully.
Trading Algorithm

The bot shall make trading decisions every 10 minutes.
Implement a simple algorithm, such as:
Buy: If the price has increased by X% in the last Y minutes.
Sell: If the price has decreased by Z% in the last Y minutes.
The parameters X%, Y minutes, and Z% should be configurable.
Simulation Engine

Start with a fictitious capital (e.g., $10,000).
Simulate buying and selling of Bitcoin based on the trading algorithm.
Keep track of the virtual portfolio, including cash balance and Bitcoin holdings.
Calculate unrealized and realized gains/losses.
Data Logging

Record all trading actions with timestamps, prices, amounts, and portfolio value.
Store logs in a structured format (e.g., CSV or JSON) for easy analysis.
Performance Reporting

Provide real-time updates on portfolio performance.
At the end of the simulation period, generate a summary report including:
Total profit or loss.
Return on investment (ROI).
Number of trades executed.
Success rate of trades.
Configuration

Allow the following parameters to be configurable:
Initial capital amount.
Trading algorithm parameters (X%, Y minutes, Z%).
Simulation duration.
API endpoints and access keys (if required).
Scheduling and Execution

The bot shall execute trading decisions precisely every 10 minutes.
Ensure accurate timing despite potential network or processing delays.
Non-Functional Requirements
Reliability

The bot must handle exceptions without crashing.
Should be able to recover from transient errors (e.g., network issues).
Performance

Efficiently process data and execute trades within the 10-minute window.
Minimal memory and CPU footprint to allow continuous running.
Usability

Clear and concise logging for ease of understanding.
Well-documented code with comments explaining key sections.
Maintainability

Modular code structure to facilitate future enhancements.
Adherence to Python coding standards (PEP 8).
Security

Secure handling of any API keys or sensitive information.
Do not hard-code sensitive data; use environment variables or configuration files.
Scalability

While the initial scope is limited, design the system to allow easy addition of features (e.g., multiple cryptocurrencies) in the future.
Assumptions and Dependencies
Assumptions

A stable internet connection is available at all times.
The API service used for price data is reliable and accessible.
The system clock is accurate for scheduling trades every 10 minutes.
Dependencies

Python 3.x environment.
External libraries for HTTP requests (e.g., requests).
Libraries for data handling (e.g., pandas).
Access to a Bitcoin price API.
Constraints
Technical Constraints

Must be developed in Python.
Limited to Bitcoin trading only.
No use of real money or integration with live trading accounts.
Operational Constraints

The bot should run on a standard computer without the need for specialized hardware.
Should not violate any terms of service of the APIs used.
User Stories
As a Developer, I want the bot to fetch real-time Bitcoin prices so that I can use up-to-date data for simulation.
As a Developer, I want to simulate trades every 10 minutes to mimic a high-frequency trading strategy.
As a Developer, I want to configure trading parameters easily so that I can test different strategies.
As a Developer, I want detailed logs of all simulated trades so that I can analyze the bot's performance.
As a Developer, I want a summary report at the end of the simulation to understand overall profitability.
Architecture Overview
Modules:

Data Fetcher: Retrieves real-time Bitcoin prices.
Trading Algorithm: Decides whether to buy, sell, or hold.
Simulation Engine: Executes simulated trades and updates portfolio.
Logger: Records trading actions and portfolio updates.
Scheduler: Ensures the trading algorithm runs every 10 minutes.
Configuration Manager: Handles configuration settings.
Data Flow:

Scheduler triggers the Trading Algorithm every 10 minutes.
The Trading Algorithm requests current price from the Data Fetcher.
Based on the algorithm, a decision is made and passed to the Simulation Engine.
The Simulation Engine updates the virtual portfolio accordingly.
The Logger records the action and updates.
After the simulation period, a report is generated.
Testing and Validation
Unit Testing
Test individual modules (Data Fetcher, Trading Algorithm, Simulation Engine) for expected behavior.
Integration Testing
Ensure modules interact correctly when combined.
Simulation Testing
Run the bot over a short period (e.g., one hour) to validate end-to-end functionality.
Performance Testing
Verify the bot can handle continuous operation without degradation.
Development Requirements
Programming Language
Python 3.x
Libraries and Tools
requests for HTTP requests.
pandas or csv module for data handling.
schedule or APScheduler for task scheduling.
Version Control
Use Git for source code management.
Documentation
Provide a README file with setup instructions.
Inline code comments for clarity.
Risks and Mitigation
Risk: API rate limiting or changes in API endpoints.

Mitigation: Implement error handling and allow API endpoints to be configurable.
Risk: Inaccurate price data due to network issues.

Mitigation: Validate data before use and implement retries on failure.
Risk: The bot stops unexpectedly.

Mitigation: Implement logging for errors and consider using a process supervisor (e.g., supervisord).
Deliverables
Python source code for the Bitcoin Trading Simulation Bot.
Configuration files with instructions on how to set parameters.
Log files of simulated trades.
Final performance report after the simulation period.
Documentation including:
Setup and installation guide.
User guide on how to run and configure the bot.
Developer notes for future enhancements.
Timeline
Week 1:

Requirements finalization and environment setup.
Develop Data Fetcher and ensure reliable price data retrieval.
Week 2:

Implement the Trading Algorithm and Simulation Engine.
Set up logging and configuration management.
Week 3:

Integrate modules and begin testing.
Run initial simulations for validation.
Week 4:

Finalize documentation.
Deploy the bot for the one-week simulation period.
Generate the performance report.
Future Enhancements
Incorporate advanced trading strategies using AI or machine learning.
Support additional cryptocurrencies.
Implement backtesting with historical data.
Develop a user interface for easier interaction.
Integrate alert systems (e.g., email or SMS notifications).
End of Document

This document outlines the full product requirements and purpose for the Bitcoin Trading Simulation Bot. It provides a comprehensive guide for software developers to understand the project's objectives, scope, and detailed specifications necessary for successful implementation.